00:27:23.758 --> 00:27:26.040
I always trying play catch up,

00:27:26.040 --> 00:27:28.470
I'm always behind, I always
trying to find my way,

00:27:28.470 --> 00:27:30.210
never get through some shit.

00:27:30.210 --> 00:27:31.073
What's going on, man, it
changed over here, man,

00:27:31.073 --> 00:27:33.790
it changed over there, man,
so-and-so ain't here no more,

00:27:33.790 --> 00:27:35.460
oh, this three ain't here
no more, oh this changed,

00:27:35.460 --> 00:27:36.810
I'm like what?

00:27:36.810 --> 00:27:38.740
I'm like, man, felt like
I was in the stone age.

00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:41.080
Every time I leave and come back home,

00:27:41.080 --> 00:27:44.210
I was getting that further,
further, further behind.

00:27:44.210 --> 00:27:47.380
I didn't have no relationship,
a real relationship

00:27:47.380 --> 00:27:49.600
with my mom, my sister, my brother.

00:27:49.600 --> 00:27:50.760
My nephews come along,

00:27:50.760 --> 00:27:52.220
I don't have no relationship with them.

00:27:52.220 --> 00:27:53.660
I'm their uncle, I love them.

00:27:53.660 --> 00:27:58.070
But I'm gone through both
of my nephews childhood.

00:27:58.070 --> 00:28:01.630
You know, and my sister
was a single parent

00:28:01.630 --> 00:28:06.630
and I was thinking man, to be an uncle,

00:28:07.530 --> 00:28:09.860
to have opportunity to
deal with my nephews.

00:28:09.860 --> 00:28:12.950
You know, it was a dream come
true when she first had Chris,

00:28:12.950 --> 00:28:14.090
excuse me, my nephew.

00:28:14.090 --> 00:28:15.830
Then we she had the other
one, it's like, wow,

00:28:15.830 --> 00:28:18.770
I wasn't there for him, but
I'ma be there for this one.

00:28:18.770 --> 00:28:19.963
That's a damn lie,

00:28:21.430 --> 00:28:24.720
because I wasn't, I didn't,
I wasn't able to be there

00:28:24.720 --> 00:28:28.547
like I wanted to, like
I needed to, you know.

00:28:28.547 --> 00:28:31.813
And they had this old saying, you know,

00:28:35.340 --> 00:28:38.880
following the footsteps of your dad,

00:28:38.880 --> 00:28:41.360
you know, and he was the absentee.

00:28:41.360 --> 00:28:43.110
And even though I didn't
have any kids on my own,

00:28:43.110 --> 00:28:45.250
I was an absentee uncle.

00:28:45.250 --> 00:28:50.250
And I thought it'd be a deterrent
for me wanting to mess up,

00:28:54.090 --> 00:28:56.680
but after about my fourth,
fifth trip to prison,

00:28:56.680 --> 00:28:58.290
I'm like, man, this shit ain't nothing,

00:28:58.290 --> 00:29:00.050
it wasn't no deterrent.

00:29:00.050 --> 00:29:01.577
Oh, man, if you do this,
you're going go to prison.

00:29:01.577 --> 00:29:05.060
Man, I don't give a fuck, I don't care,

00:29:05.060 --> 00:29:06.940
prison don't scare me.

00:29:06.940 --> 00:29:08.760
Smoke all the crack in California,

00:29:08.760 --> 00:29:10.990
drink all the drinks, smoke all the weed.

00:29:10.990 --> 00:29:12.930
Rob, still do what I do.

00:29:12.930 --> 00:29:16.420
'cause it wasn't no
determined, it wasn't a factor

00:29:17.360 --> 00:29:22.160
in me wanting to change and
try something different,

00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:24.907
because by then, man, I was in too deep

00:29:24.907 --> 00:29:26.430
and I was lost in a sauce, man.

00:29:26.430 --> 00:29:30.433
So, even though now in retrospect,

00:29:34.836 --> 00:29:37.260
man, I just went to that plantation, bro.

00:29:37.260 --> 00:29:39.890
I went to the plantation, yes sir,

00:29:39.890 --> 00:29:43.400
and I had to do they
motherfucking bidding, yes sir.

00:29:43.400 --> 00:29:46.773
For a little bit of
nothing and I better did.

00:29:48.083 --> 00:29:50.360
And if I didn't do it, there
were some consequences,

00:29:50.360 --> 00:29:53.350
you know, all that kind of stuff, any who.

00:29:53.350 --> 00:29:57.750
Man, so, I'm back and forth, you know,

00:29:57.750 --> 00:30:01.363
working in the kitchen,
working for 3 cents, 5 cents,

00:30:01.363 --> 00:30:03.290
7 cents an hour, you know.

00:30:03.290 --> 00:30:06.100
At the end of the month
I get $14, you know,

00:30:06.100 --> 00:30:06.940
I'm think I'm balling.

00:30:06.940 --> 00:30:08.800
Wow, it's time to go to the canteen.

00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:10.330
Porters fill out your canteen slip, man,

00:30:10.330 --> 00:30:12.540
kitchen workers go early, we go first.

00:30:12.540 --> 00:30:13.976
You know, 'cause you guys, you know,

00:30:13.976 --> 00:30:16.373
service is up in here.

00:30:16.373 --> 00:30:17.260
You know, you serve the people

00:30:17.260 --> 00:30:18.310
and all that kinds of stuff, the inmates.

00:30:18.310 --> 00:30:20.030
Okay, that's cool, that's cool.

00:30:20.030 --> 00:30:21.410
You know, and get my little soups

00:30:21.410 --> 00:30:24.046
and my little few bag of
chips and my honey buns.

00:30:24.046 --> 00:30:27.430
And I'm like, wow, you know, I'm good.

00:30:27.430 --> 00:30:30.000
You know, but I had a place

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.853
where I can go where I feel safe.

00:30:33.240 --> 00:30:35.170
I had to worry about stuff,
but not to the degree

00:30:35.170 --> 00:30:37.360
as on the streets, I didn't have the crack

00:30:37.360 --> 00:30:39.840
around me, messing with
me and driving me crazy,

00:30:39.840 --> 00:30:41.630
'cause I just had to have that shit

00:30:41.630 --> 00:30:42.680
and I couldn't live without it.

00:30:42.680 --> 00:30:44.430
I could live with it or without it.

00:30:46.400 --> 00:30:47.830
I didn't have relationship with nobody

00:30:47.830 --> 00:30:49.580
in my immediate family.

00:30:49.580 --> 00:30:53.290
So, when I'm going to prison,
I just read, read, work out

00:30:53.290 --> 00:30:55.700
and worked in a kitchen, you know.

00:30:55.700 --> 00:30:59.640
And out of all those trips to prison man,

00:30:59.640 --> 00:31:01.530
I learned that, there was some things

00:31:01.530 --> 00:31:03.667
that I had to address
when I was there, man.

00:31:03.667 --> 00:31:05.863
And the biggest one
for me was self-hatred.

00:31:08.270 --> 00:31:11.300
I wouldn't admit it, but I hate it man,

00:31:11.300 --> 00:31:13.630
I hated me, I hated being black,

00:31:13.630 --> 00:31:16.833
because of the circumstances,
man, that I was brought up in.

00:31:17.850 --> 00:31:18.950
Yeah, you tell me how I'm doing,

00:31:18.950 --> 00:31:21.380
no, I'm good, man, I'm fine,
yeah, everything is okay,

00:31:21.380 --> 00:31:24.130
soul brother, peace and all that bullshit.

00:31:24.130 --> 00:31:27.103
Truth be told, I couldn't
stand being black,

00:31:28.200 --> 00:31:30.793
poor and in real trouble.

00:31:32.790 --> 00:31:35.330
You know, and I just saw
the writing on a wall, man.

00:31:35.330 --> 00:31:38.450
I'm like, Oh man, I see
what I'm destined for.

00:31:38.450 --> 00:31:39.790
By the way things are lining up

00:31:39.790 --> 00:31:43.760
and I saw that shit early
on in the game, saw it.

00:31:43.760 --> 00:31:46.603
It wasn't nothing that can
stop me from going that route.

00:31:49.770 --> 00:31:50.630
I didn't have enough role models,

00:31:50.630 --> 00:31:52.590
didn't have enough people that really care

00:31:52.590 --> 00:31:53.423
about the next man.

00:31:53.423 --> 00:31:54.970
We was all in the same boat,

00:31:54.970 --> 00:31:57.230
everybody was poor and
discordant and depressed

00:31:57.230 --> 00:31:58.483
and all that bullshit.

00:31:59.330 --> 00:32:01.550
We wouldn't talk about it as kids.

00:32:01.550 --> 00:32:03.100
You know, running around with holey shoes

00:32:03.100 --> 00:32:05.690
and all that bullshit, hand
me down clothes and all that.

00:32:05.690 --> 00:32:07.370
I remember I used to walk to school,

00:32:07.370 --> 00:32:09.810
walking to school sliding my foot,

00:32:09.810 --> 00:32:12.390
because in both of my
shoes, I had big ass holes

00:32:12.390 --> 00:32:16.250
at the bottom of them, I used
to put newspaper court board.

00:32:16.250 --> 00:32:18.870
So, I'm walking to school,
one and slide in the one.

00:32:18.870 --> 00:32:21.100
Soon as I would lift my foot up,

00:32:21.100 --> 00:32:23.900
somebody it get them talking

00:32:23.900 --> 00:32:25.660
and they'd get the laugh and a clowning

00:32:25.660 --> 00:32:27.043
and all that kind of stuff.

00:32:28.210 --> 00:32:31.220
Man, I used to like hate that shit man,

00:32:31.220 --> 00:32:33.630
And having pants that were too small,

00:32:33.630 --> 00:32:35.410
so, I have to wear them way down here,

00:32:35.410 --> 00:32:37.350
at they call sagging today,
but I was doing that shit

00:32:37.350 --> 00:32:39.920
way back in the days, because
the pants were hand me down,

00:32:39.920 --> 00:32:42.963
they were given to me, you know, so,

00:32:46.590 --> 00:32:48.760
having other kids and look
at me a certain kind of way

00:32:48.760 --> 00:32:49.593
when I'm in school,

00:32:49.593 --> 00:32:51.470
'cause I was busted to the Valley schools.

00:32:51.470 --> 00:32:54.480
So, they used to give me that look.

00:32:54.480 --> 00:32:56.720
And I knew what that look meant, you know,

00:32:56.720 --> 00:32:59.260
Oh, feel sorry for this dude.

00:32:59.260 --> 00:33:01.160
You see how those little lunch things,

00:33:02.350 --> 00:33:05.670
for food, you know, for the
lunches and breakfast and stuff.

00:33:05.670 --> 00:33:07.880
And people used to get on the other side

00:33:07.880 --> 00:33:09.680
with their little change and dollars.

00:33:09.680 --> 00:33:12.730
And used to get over here
with the meal tickets man.

00:33:12.730 --> 00:33:16.930
And wasn't no shame in
the game or nothing,

00:33:16.930 --> 00:33:18.510
you know, 'cause I ain't tripping.

00:33:18.510 --> 00:33:20.640
You know, shit, free, paid, don't matter.

00:33:20.640 --> 00:33:22.520
You know, if I had some change,

00:33:22.520 --> 00:33:23.530
I'd rather use the ticket,

00:33:23.530 --> 00:33:25.250
because I can keep the
little dollar and a quarter,

00:33:25.250 --> 00:33:28.670
whatever it was, you know, that
I saved from not buying it.

00:33:28.670 --> 00:33:30.170
So, that really didn't bother me.

00:33:30.170 --> 00:33:33.080
But just the looks that
I got, knowing that

00:33:36.060 --> 00:33:41.060
it wasn't so much as how they
saw me, or what they said

00:33:41.220 --> 00:33:43.460
or what they thought, but more so,

00:33:43.460 --> 00:33:45.730
what I've thought and felt about me.

00:33:45.730 --> 00:33:48.217
And that's where the self
hatred came in there.

00:33:48.217 --> 00:33:49.740
'cause there was in the gut,

00:33:49.740 --> 00:33:52.670
there wasn't a damn
thing I can do about it.

00:33:52.670 --> 00:33:54.710
You know, and the only
thing I could do was run.

00:33:54.710 --> 00:33:57.823
Tuck my tail and run
and I just added to it.

00:33:58.680 --> 00:34:00.365
I couldn't stand up for myself.

00:34:00.365 --> 00:34:04.210
I couldn't fight for me or nothing,

00:34:04.210 --> 00:34:07.193
unless I had the marijuana, the alcohol,

00:34:08.140 --> 00:34:11.040
you know, and whatever that
would induce with the crack,

00:34:11.040 --> 00:34:13.230
that just amplified all the other stuff

00:34:13.230 --> 00:34:15.620
that I was holding in, you know.

00:34:15.620 --> 00:34:18.720
So, on that shit just
almost drove me crazy,

00:34:18.720 --> 00:34:21.283
you know, because I
just couldn't, you know,

00:34:21.283 --> 00:34:23.770
I smoke so much man, and did so much, man.

00:34:23.770 --> 00:34:25.590
But if it wasn't for prison,

00:34:25.590 --> 00:34:28.450
I would have been dead or
would have been on deed

00:34:28.450 --> 00:34:30.600
and that's the God's honest truth.

00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:33.170
Prison saved my life.

00:34:33.170 --> 00:34:36.643
And then, in another sense, you know,

00:34:36.643 --> 00:34:40.303
I found myself in there, I found me.

00:34:41.620 --> 00:34:44.720
You know, 'cause I ran
there thinking I was hiding

00:34:44.720 --> 00:34:48.700
and escaping my reality,

00:34:48.700 --> 00:34:50.640
but that's where I found solace man.

00:34:50.640 --> 00:34:53.490
That's where I had time to
really do some soul searching.

00:34:54.690 --> 00:34:56.700
I remember one year I went to prison,

00:34:56.700 --> 00:34:58.620
I think it was, I forgotten.

00:34:58.620 --> 00:35:00.790
Anyway, I read all black history books,

00:35:00.790 --> 00:35:03.790
Before the Mayflower, The Middle
Passage and all that stuff.

00:35:05.200 --> 00:35:07.950
I said, wow man, great contributions.

00:35:07.950 --> 00:35:10.090
This, this, I said, wow.

00:35:10.090 --> 00:35:14.190
And that kind of changed my mind about me,

00:35:14.190 --> 00:35:17.537
because in school,
being been busted Valley

00:35:17.537 --> 00:35:20.070
and all white folks, we reading,

00:35:20.070 --> 00:35:23.450
this is elementary, junior
high, history books.

00:35:23.450 --> 00:35:26.720
The first two pages of
every book was on slavery.

00:35:26.720 --> 00:35:31.260
The first two pages, slavery.

00:35:31.260 --> 00:35:34.690
So, I'm two, three black
kids up in here, man.

00:35:34.690 --> 00:35:36.773
And we reading about this shit.

00:35:37.850 --> 00:35:39.530
If I can turn red, I
would have turned red,

00:35:39.530 --> 00:35:42.640
but I think I must have
turned purple every time

00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:46.210
the history class re-read
about the slavery.

00:35:46.210 --> 00:35:47.210
Man, that was the first,

00:35:47.210 --> 00:35:49.545
the beginning of every history book, man,

00:35:49.545 --> 00:35:51.943
that's what started with, I'm like, God.

00:35:53.080 --> 00:35:55.540
I say, can't they put this in
the middle, towards the end,

00:35:55.540 --> 00:35:57.697
because this is the
starting off place, man,

00:35:57.697 --> 00:35:59.313
and all eyes is on me.

00:36:01.710 --> 00:36:03.643
I'm like, uh, duh.

00:36:05.157 --> 00:36:07.350
And I hated that, I hated it, man,

00:36:07.350 --> 00:36:10.070
I hated being in that predicament man,

00:36:10.070 --> 00:36:12.640
of being one of the few
token black kids man,

00:36:12.640 --> 00:36:13.943
at this white school, man.

00:36:14.940 --> 00:36:18.060
In history class, speaking on,

00:36:18.060 --> 00:36:20.210
it just does something to me, man.

00:36:20.210 --> 00:36:22.640
And even to this day, it bothers me,

00:36:22.640 --> 00:36:24.910
but not as much as it did back then.

00:36:24.910 --> 00:36:27.560
I didn't have nobody to talk to back then.

00:36:27.560 --> 00:36:29.390
You know, I didn't mess with nobody

00:36:29.390 --> 00:36:32.120
in elementary and junior high,
I was alone that end too.

00:36:32.120 --> 00:36:34.540
I stayed to myself, did my own thing,

00:36:34.540 --> 00:36:36.210
talk to a few people, but pretty much

00:36:36.210 --> 00:36:37.780
didn't building no relationships
and nothing like that,

00:36:37.780 --> 00:36:40.050
didn't have no friends back then.

00:36:40.050 --> 00:36:43.303
But, yeah man, it was just,

00:36:44.420 --> 00:36:46.540
in prison I read all those books,

00:36:46.540 --> 00:36:48.933
start to see things different and then,

00:36:51.430 --> 00:36:53.810
I guess when the student's
ready, the teacher appears.

00:36:53.810 --> 00:36:55.823
So, I think after like,

00:36:57.090 --> 00:37:00.370
19 trips to prison, my saving grace.

00:37:00.370 --> 00:37:03.043
Thank you, I didn't say it
back then, but now I do.

00:37:06.753 --> 00:37:11.000
I was really ready for that
change from the inside out.

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:12.560
I knew something had to be different,

00:37:12.560 --> 00:37:14.600
because I have been going so many times.

00:37:14.600 --> 00:37:17.620
I knew if something didn't
happen this last time,

00:37:17.620 --> 00:37:21.220
that I was just gonna be,

00:37:21.220 --> 00:37:23.610
that's it, it's a wrap, you know.

00:37:23.610 --> 00:37:28.610
And what happened was,
the last time, you know,

00:37:28.850 --> 00:37:31.530
I went to the same prison
three times in a row.

00:37:31.530 --> 00:37:33.723
went back to back, to back, to back,

00:37:34.560 --> 00:37:37.770
same one, back, back, back, the same one.

00:37:37.770 --> 00:37:39.880
So, all three times that
they see me come and go,

00:37:39.880 --> 00:37:42.593
see me come, like damn,
you're back again, yeah.

00:37:45.299 --> 00:37:47.933
The third time, I did the same thing

00:37:48.840 --> 00:37:50.210
I did the other two times.

00:37:50.210 --> 00:37:53.620
I did the self-help classes,
I did the Islamic services,

00:37:53.620 --> 00:37:55.690
I did the church, I did all that stuff.

00:37:55.690 --> 00:37:58.480
Worked out like I did, I've been doing,

00:37:58.480 --> 00:38:00.450
'cause it worked for me, it helped me.

00:38:00.450 --> 00:38:04.970
Shit, I'm not gonna stop
doing what helped me

00:38:04.970 --> 00:38:06.130
while I was in there.

00:38:06.130 --> 00:38:09.360
I went to the library, I read
all the books that I can find.

00:38:09.360 --> 00:38:10.620
I love autobiographies.

00:38:10.620 --> 00:38:12.620
I got burnt out on black history,

00:38:12.620 --> 00:38:16.160
because my whole prison term,
I read none but that, so,

00:38:16.160 --> 00:38:19.210
I was like, I'm good, I don't
have to read another page,

00:38:19.210 --> 00:38:21.220
I don't have to hear
about another contribution

00:38:21.220 --> 00:38:23.020
that we made back, I'm good.

00:38:23.020 --> 00:38:26.270
You know, I'm good, I'm okay with me now.

00:38:26.270 --> 00:38:29.380
You know, so, the self-hatred left me,

00:38:29.380 --> 00:38:31.450
but I carried that a long time.

00:38:31.450 --> 00:38:34.930
And I used to trip on how, even down here

00:38:34.930 --> 00:38:38.326
when I see the young black
men and I see that look.

00:38:38.326 --> 00:38:41.393
Oh, I know that look, I had the same look.

00:38:42.320 --> 00:38:45.940
I had that same look, anger, the despair,

00:38:45.940 --> 00:38:50.060
I'm gonna tear somebody's
head off, that was me.

00:38:50.060 --> 00:38:53.240
I know what it is 'cause
I went through it.

00:38:53.240 --> 00:38:58.010
Made it to the other side, what
a blessing, what a blessing.

00:38:59.660 --> 00:39:02.070
But self realization is the best one.

00:39:02.070 --> 00:39:03.120
And only way you're going to learn that

00:39:03.120 --> 00:39:04.240
is by your own experience,

00:39:04.240 --> 00:39:07.280
'cause your own experience is
gonna be your best teacher.

00:39:07.280 --> 00:39:09.640
I read many books on black history,

00:39:09.640 --> 00:39:13.740
but me living as a black man
in California, Los Angeles.

00:39:13.740 --> 00:39:15.510
Back in the time of the gangs,

00:39:15.510 --> 00:39:18.410
the crack and all that bullshit epidemics.

00:39:18.410 --> 00:39:22.843
You know, man, that's a
story in itself, you know,

00:39:25.600 --> 00:39:30.100
I should write a book
on surviving the streets

00:39:31.370 --> 00:39:36.370
of Los Angeles during the 80s,
that worst time of my life.

00:39:36.600 --> 00:39:41.050
And it was out of my control, you know.

00:39:41.050 --> 00:39:43.810
And, so, what happened was, man,

00:39:43.810 --> 00:39:45.310
the last time something had to happen

00:39:45.310 --> 00:39:46.780
and I did everything I did the last time,

00:39:46.780 --> 00:39:48.510
but it said, when the students are ready

00:39:48.510 --> 00:39:50.220
the teacher will appear.

00:39:50.220 --> 00:39:54.090
And lo and behold, I had many
teachers appear my last term

00:39:54.950 --> 00:39:57.870
